// Base-128 varints, and the zigzag transform that goes with them:
// https://protobuf.dev/programming-guides/encoding/#varints
//
// Seven bits per octet, least significant group first, the high bit marking that more
// follow. protobuf calls it "Base 128 Varints" and DWARF calls it unsigned LEB128; they
// are the same encoding.
//
// Zigzag is separate because it is a transform on the value rather than an encoding of
// it: it folds a signed number onto an unsigned one so a small negative stays short.
